host byte order to network byte order. To facilitate this, the socket API provides the functions
htons and htonl:
uint16_t htons( uint16_t hostshort );
uint32_t htonl( uint32_t hostlong );
The htons function takes any unsigned, 16-bit integer in the host’s native byte order and
converts it to the same integer represented in the network’s native byte order. The htonl
function performs the same operation on 32-bit integers.
